def LAD(*a): return list(a)
def RUB(a,b,c,d): return [(a,'Missing or unclear','Meets the stated check',b),(c,'Guessing','Evidence kept',d),('Records','Gaps','Complete','Complete and reviewed by a peer'),('Safety and ethics','Overlooked','Followed','Followed and taught to others')]
COURSES = [
dict(slug='training-and-development', title='Training and Development Practice', level='L4 Practitioner',
 summary='Plan, deliver and measure workplace training that changes what people do on the job, from the first needs check to a 30-day follow-up with numbers.',
 outs=[('Define','a training need as task, condition and standard, backed by records.'),('Apply','objectives, a timed plan and active practice to a real session.'),('Analyse','assessment and job data to see what changed.'),('Evaluate','a session using four levels of evidence.'),('Create','a two-hour course with materials, a checklist and a follow-up plan.')],
 task='Design, deliver and evaluate a two-hour training session for a real work need, and report results 30 days later.', cond='About 8 weeks part-time. A group of 8 to 15 learners, a room or online space, a projector or board, printed checklists, a mentor.',
 standard='Every objective has an action verb and a measure; every activity links to an objective; at least 80% of learners meet the checklist standard; a 30-day follow-up shows a measured change in a work number.', who='Trainers, team leaders, HR staff, supervisors, teachers moving into industry.', req='None. Experience of any workplace helps.',
 mods=[
 M('Find the training need','Analyse',5,['Separate a knowledge gap (they do not know how) from a motivation gap (they know but do not) and a system gap (tools or rules block them); training fixes only the first.','Gather evidence from three sources: records, direct observation of five tasks, and short talks with five workers and their supervisor.','Write the need as task, condition and standard, for example: record a stock-out within 10 minutes using the register.','Estimate the cost of the gap in rupees or hours so the sponsor can see why it matters.'],'A shop chain finds 18 of 60 billing errors a week come from wrong discount entry. Observation shows 4 of 5 cashiers never learned the discount screen. Gap cost: 18 errors x Rs 150 average loss = Rs 2,700 a week. Need: enter a discount correctly in under 30 seconds.','Write a needs statement for a real group, with three pieces of evidence and a weekly cost of the gap.','Statement has task, condition and standard, three evidence sources, and a cost figure.','How do you know a problem is not a training problem?','If workers know how but tools, rules or rewards stop them, it is a system or motivation gap.'),
 M('Write objectives','Apply',4,['Use one observable verb per objective: list, demonstrate, calculate, compare, evaluate, design.','Add a measure: number correct, time limit or accuracy, for example 5 of 6 steps in order.','Avoid verbs you cannot see, such as understand, know or appreciate.','Match each objective to one assessment task so nothing is taught that is not checked.'],'Weak: understand fire safety. Strong: list the 5 steps to use an extinguisher in order without notes, and demonstrate pulling the pin and aiming at the base of the fire in under 20 seconds.','Write five objectives for your session and pair each with its assessment task.','All five have an action verb, a measure and a matching assessment.','Why is the word understand a poor objective verb?','It cannot be observed or measured, so you cannot tell if the objective was met.'),
 M('Plan the session','Create',6,['Use the order open, teach, practise, check, close, with practice taking at least half of the time.','Time every step and keep 5 to 10 minutes of slack; prepare one spare activity and one cut-down option.','List materials, room layout and printouts per learner, and test every item the day before.','Use two worked examples: one shown by you, one done by learners with you watching.'],'A 120-minute plan: 10 open with a real problem, 20 teach with a worked example, 60 practise in pairs, 15 check with a checklist, 10 close with action plans, 5 slack. Materials: 15 checklists, 15 practice sheets, 1 spare case study.','Build a timed plan with a materials list for your two-hour session.','Times add to 120 minutes, each step links to an objective, and materials are listed.','Why keep slack time in a plan?','Learners and equipment are unpredictable, and slack prevents rushing the practice.'),
 M('Deliver with confidence','Apply',5,['Stand where all can see you, speak at a steady pace, pause after each question for five seconds.','Use names and ask open questions; invite quiet learners by asking for an example from their own work.','Handle a dominant speaker by thanking them and asking someone else to add a view.','Use a story from the learner\'s own work, not a distant example, to link new skills to daily tasks.'],'A trainer asks a quiet cashier, Tell me about the last time a customer asked for a discount, then writes the steps she describes on the board. Learner talk time rises from 20% to about 60%.','Deliver a 20-minute segment to peers and collect notes from two observers.','Peer notes name two strengths and one change; the change is tried in a second delivery.','What can you do when one learner talks too much?','Thank them, then ask others for a view or give each person a turn.'),
 M('Online and blended delivery','Apply',4,['Cut content into chunks of 10 to 15 minutes and add a poll, a question or a task between chunks.','Give instructions in text and voice, and say what the output must look like and by when.','Test the link, sound, screen sharing and a low-bandwidth plan on a mobile network before the day.','Keep a helper to answer chat and admit people, so you can focus on teaching.'],'A 60-minute online session: 12 minutes teach, 3 minutes poll, 12 minutes breakout task, 10 minutes share, 12 minutes teach, 11 minutes practice and close. Audio fails for 2 learners, so the helper shares the slides as a downloaded file.','Convert a 30-minute segment to an online format and run a test with two people.','Chunks are no longer than 15 minutes and the test run works on a mobile connection.','How long should an online teaching chunk be before an activity?','About ten to fifteen minutes.'),
 M('Assess learning','Evaluate',5,['Use an observation checklist of 4 to 6 observable steps and mark each step done or not done.','Check during the session with quick questions, and after it with a short practical task.','Give feedback that names one thing done well, one step missed and one way to fix it.','Set a pass line before the session, for example 5 of 6 steps, and record results by learner.'],'Checklist for entering a discount: opens screen, selects item, enters percent, checks total, prints bill, files copy. 12 of 15 learners complete 5 or more steps (80%). Three missed the total check; they get a 10-minute re-practice.','Build a checklist and mark two learners, giving feedback to each.','Checklist items are observable and feedback names a specific step.','What three things should feedback include?','What was done well, which step was missed and how to improve it.'),
 M('Measure results','Evaluate',5,['Use four levels: reaction (did they like it), learning (can they do it), behaviour (do they do it at work), results (did a business number move).','Collect reaction in the last 5 minutes with a 3-question form; collect behaviour 30 days later by observing five tasks.','Compare a before and an after number, for example errors per week, and note other changes that could explain it.','Be honest in reports: say what is measured and what is a guess.'],'Before: 18 discount errors a week. After 30 days: 5 errors. Reduction: 13 errors x Rs 150 = Rs 1,950 saved a week. Session cost Rs 6,000, so payback in about 3 weeks. Cashier turnover also fell, so the report notes this as a possible second cause.','Write a measurement plan with a tool, date and owner for each of the four levels.','Plan has a named measure and date for each level, plus one caution about other causes.','Name the four levels of evaluation.','Reaction, learning, behaviour and results.'),
 M('Capstone: run and report','Create',6,['Deliver your two-hour session to at least 8 learners using your plan.','Collect reaction forms, checklist marks and, after 30 days, one work number.','Write a one-page report with objectives, data, three improvements and next steps.','Present the report to peers and a mentor and take questions.'],'Report: 12 learners, 10 met the standard (83%), average reaction 4.4 out of 5, errors fell from 18 to 5 a week. Improvements: more practice time, a pocket guide, a refresher at week 6.','Deliver, measure and present the report.','Report has all four levels of evidence and three improvements; at least 80% met the standard.','What makes a training report credible?','It shows measured data at several levels and admits what is not known.')],
 extra=[('Why plan spare activities?','Time and learner pace vary, and spare tasks prevent gaps or rushing.'),('When do you follow up on the job?','About thirty days later, once learners have had time to use the skill.')],
 rubric=RUB('Objectives','Objectives measurable and linked to assessment','Delivery','Delivery adapted to the group and timed'),
 ladder=LAD('Know what a training session is.','Describe how adults learn.','Deliver a short session using a plan.','Design and run a full session alone.','Design programmes, coach trainers and measure results.','Lead a training function with budgets and standards.','Set learning strategy and standards for an organisation.'),
 jobs=['Trainer','Learning and development coordinator','Instructional designer','Team leader who coaches','Freelance trainer']),

dict(slug='attire-and-accessories', title='Attire and Accessories Business', level='L4 Practitioner',
 summary='Plan, source, make or sell clothing and accessories for a local market, with correct costing, written quality checks, honest descriptions and fair practice.',
 outs=[('Define','target customers and product lines with size and price range.'),('Apply','costing and pricing to each product.'),('Analyse','fabric, fit and finish against a quality checklist.'),('Evaluate','suppliers, returns and margins.'),('Create','a five-product collection with a selling plan.')],
 task='Develop a small collection of five products with cost sheets, quality checks, honest listings and a selling plan.', cond='About 10 weeks part-time. Fabric swatches, a measuring tape, a kitchen scale, a phone camera, a sewing or sourcing contact, a mentor.',
 standard='Each product has a full cost sheet where price covers cost plus at least 30% margin, passes a written quality checklist, and has a listing that matches the real item.', who='Designers, tailors, shop owners, online sellers, students.', req='None.',
 mods=[
 M('Choose customers and product lines','Define',4,['Describe one customer in detail: age, work, budget, occasions and where she or he shops.','Pick a line of 5 related products, for example cotton kurtas, stoles, tote bags, belts and hair accessories.','Check demand by visiting 3 shops and 3 online listings and noting price, size range and colour.','Choose a season: festive, summer, wedding or school, and plan stock for it.'],'Customer: working woman aged 25 to 35, spends Rs 800 to Rs 1,500 on a kurta, wears them 4 days a week. Line: 3 cotton kurtas, 1 stole, 1 tote. Three shops sell similar kurtas at Rs 899, Rs 1,099 and Rs 1,299.','Write a one-page customer profile and line plan with price bands.','Profile has budget, occasion and a price band for every product.','Why choose one customer first?','Designs, prices and sales channels all follow from knowing who will buy.'),
 M('Know fabrics and trims','Analyse',5,['Identify common fabrics: cotton, linen, rayon, polyester, silk blends and leather or faux leather, by feel, burn-free tests and labels.','Test a swatch for shrinkage by marking 10 cm squares, washing and measuring; more than 3% shrinkage needs pre-washing.','Test colour run by soaking a swatch in warm water on white cloth for 10 minutes.','Match fabric to use: breathable cotton for daily wear, stiff fabric for bags, soft lining for stoles.'],'A 10 cm cotton swatch measures 9.5 cm after washing: shrinkage 5%. A 3 m kurta length will lose about 15 cm, so the pattern adds 5% allowance or the fabric is pre-washed.','Test three swatches for shrinkage and colour run and record the results.','Results are in a table with percent shrinkage and a pass or fail for colour.','What does 5% shrinkage mean for a 100 cm length?','It will shrink about 5 cm.'),
 M('Measure and fit','Apply',5,['Take body measures with the tape snug but not tight: bust, waist, hip, shoulder, sleeve and length.','Build a size chart with S, M, L, XL based on measures plus ease of 4 to 6 cm for comfort.','Make or buy a sample, try it on two people of different shapes and note pulling or gaping.','Print the size chart in centimetres on every listing and tag.'],'Medium kurta: bust 92 cm body plus 6 cm ease gives a garment bust of 98 cm; length 100 cm; sleeve 20 cm. Fit test on two people shows tightness under the arm, so armhole depth increases by 1.5 cm.','Build a four-size chart and fit-test one sample on two people.','Chart lists body and garment measures, and the fit notes lead to one change.','Why add ease to body measures?','So the wearer can move and breathe comfortably.'),
 M('Cost each product','Apply',6,['List fabric, lining, trims, thread, labels, tailoring labour, packing and a share of rent, power and transport.','Add wastage of 5 to 10% on fabric and rejects, and a share of unsold stock.','Divide monthly overheads by the number of pieces made to get overhead per piece.','Round the final cost up and keep the sheet in a file for every product.'],'Kurta: fabric 2.5 m at Rs 120 = Rs 300; wastage 8% = Rs 24; trims Rs 30; tailoring Rs 180; packing Rs 20; overhead Rs 4,000 / 100 pieces = Rs 40. Total cost = Rs 594.','Build cost sheets for all five products.','Sheets list every cost line, wastage and overhead, and totals are correct.','Why include wastage in the cost?','Cut-offs and rejects are real costs you must recover.'),
 M('Set prices and margin','Evaluate',5,['Margin is profit divided by selling price; markup is profit divided by cost; do not mix them.','Target at least 30% margin after discounts, marketplace fees and returns.','Check the price against three competitors and against your customer budget.','Plan discount rules in advance, such as 10% for festive sale, and recheck the margin.'],'Cost Rs 594. Price Rs 999. Profit Rs 405, margin 405 / 999 = 40.5%. After a 10% festival discount: price Rs 899, profit Rs 305, margin 33.9%, still above 30%.','Set a price for each product and calculate margin with and without a discount.','Each product meets 30% margin after the largest planned discount.','If cost is Rs 600 and price Rs 1,000, what is the margin?','Profit Rs 400 divided by price Rs 1,000 is 40%.'),
 M('Control quality','Evaluate',5,['Write a checklist: straight seams, 8 to 10 stitches per inch, no loose threads, matching pattern, working zips and snaps, correct size tag.','Inspect each piece under good light and use a measure to check key dimensions within 1 cm.','Record defects in a log with type, cause and fix; investigate any defect seen in 3 or more pieces.','Pack in clean bags and keep damp pieces away from stock.'],'Batch of 40 kurtas: 3 show uneven hems, 2 have loose buttons. Defect rate 5 of 40 = 12.5%. Cause: tailor fatigue near end of day. Fix: hem check at mid-batch; next batch has 1 defect (2.5%).','Inspect five pieces with your checklist and log every defect.','Log shows defect type, count, cause and a fix.','What do you do when the same defect appears three times?','Find the cause and fix the process, not just the piece.'),
 M('Source and select suppliers','Evaluate',4,['Collect quotes from at least three suppliers for the same fabric with price, minimum order and delivery time.','Ask for a swatch and test it before ordering the full quantity.','Check fair practice: no child labour, fair wages, and safe workshop conditions.','Pay on written terms and keep invoices and bills for tax and returns.'],'Supplier A: Rs 110 per metre, 50 m minimum, 10 days. Supplier B: Rs 118, 20 m minimum, 5 days. For a 40 m first batch, B costs Rs 4,720 and arrives sooner; A needs a 50 m order costing Rs 5,500. B is chosen.','Compare three suppliers for one material in a table and choose one with reasons.','Table shows price, minimum, time and the test result for each.','Why test a swatch before a bulk order?','To avoid shrinking, colour run or poor quality across the whole batch.'),
 M('Capstone: collection and selling plan','Create',6,['Finish five products with cost sheets, size charts and a quality log.','Photograph each in daylight, front, back and detail, with a true colour.','Write honest listings with fabric, size, care, price and return rules.','Plan channels, a launch month and a target for units and profit.'],'Collection of 5 products, average price Rs 899, average margin 36%. Launch plan: 100 pieces in month 1 through a social page and two stalls, target profit Rs 30,000, returns kept under 5%.','Present the collection, sample pieces and the selling plan.','Every product has cost sheet, passed checklist and honest listing; plan has numbers.','What makes a listing honest?','It shows true colour, real measures, fabric and care, and clear return rules.')],
 extra=[('What is margin?','Profit as a share of the selling price.'),('Why test fabric before sewing?','To avoid shrinking and colour run after the garment is made.')],
 rubric=RUB('Costing','Every cost line, wastage and overhead included','Quality','Quality system with defect trends and fixes'),
 ladder=LAD('Know garment parts and fabric types.','Explain fabric, fit and care.','Make and sell simple items.','Run a small line with costing and checks.','Lead collections and supplier systems.','Lead a brand team across channels.','Set standards across a regional brand.'),
 jobs=['Tailor or maker','Fashion assistant','Boutique owner','Quality checker','Online seller']),

dict(slug='home-improvement', title='Home Improvement and Smart Living', level='L4 Practitioner',
 summary='Plan and carry out safe small home improvements, from repairs and painting to energy savings and simple smart devices, with correct measures, safety steps and a clear quote.',
 outs=[('Define','common home systems: water, power, walls and ventilation.'),('Apply','safe tool use and isolation steps.'),('Analyse','a home problem to find its cause.'),('Evaluate','cost, payback and risk of a fix.'),('Create','a job plan with measurements, materials and a quote.')],
 task='Plan a small home improvement job, with measurements, materials list, safety steps, schedule and an itemised quote.', cond='About 8 weeks part-time. Hand tools, tape, spirit level, a voltage tester, a real or model room, a mentor.',
 standard='Measures are within 3 mm, materials include 10% wastage, every risk has a control before work starts, and the quote matches the plan line by line.', who='Homeowners, tenants, handymen, small contractors, facility staff.', req='None. Never work on live mains power.',
 mods=[
 M('Know the home systems','Define',4,['Trace the water line from tank or meter to taps, and locate the main stop valve.','Locate the main switch, the distribution board, circuit breakers and the earth connection.','Note how walls are built (brick, concrete, drywall) and where ventilation and drainage run.','Draw a simple plan showing each system and mark where pipes and cables are likely hidden.'],'A 2-bedroom flat has one main switch, 6 breakers (lights, fans, 2 socket circuits, kitchen, bathroom geyser), and the main water valve under the kitchen sink. Pipes run along the bathroom wall facing the kitchen.','Draw a labelled plan of your own room or a model room.','Plan locates the main switch, main valve and at least four hidden-run risks.','Why locate the main valve and main switch first?','So you can shut off water or power quickly in an emergency or before work.'),
 M('Use tools safely','Apply',5,['Match the tool to the task: right size screwdriver, spanner, hammer, drill bit and saw.','Wear eye protection, gloves, dust mask and sturdy shoes for drilling, cutting or sanding.','Inspect tools before use: no cracked handles, frayed cords or blunt blades.','Keep the work area clear, use a stable ladder on firm floor and have someone hold it.'],'Drilling a 6 mm hole in a concrete wall: use a 6 mm masonry bit, mark the depth with tape at 40 mm, wear goggles and mask, and check the wall with a detector for pipes first.','Complete a tool and PPE checklist and demonstrate three tool tasks under supervision.','Checklist is complete and every task is done with correct PPE.','What do you check before using a power tool?','The cord, plug, blade or bit, and guards; and that PPE is worn.'),
 M('Isolate power and work near electricity','Apply',5,['Switch off at the breaker, then test the wire with a voltage tester to confirm it is dead before touching.','Lock or tag the breaker so no one switches it on while you work.','Never touch exposed wires with wet hands; keep water away from sockets and switches.','Hire a licensed electrician for any change to the distribution board or fixed wiring.'],'Replacing a ceiling fan regulator: breaker for the fan circuit off, tester shows no voltage on both wires, breaker taped with a note. Work takes 30 minutes; power returns only after the cover is fitted.','Practise the isolate, test and tag sequence on a model board.','Each step is done in order and tester is checked on a known live source first.','What proves a wire is safe to touch?','A voltage tester showing no voltage after the breaker is off.'),
 M('Measure and mark accurately','Apply',5,['Measure twice, write the figure down and mark with a pencil.','Use a spirit level for straight and plumb lines, and a square for right angles.','Allow for wastage of 10% on tiles, paint, boards and pipe.','Convert room sizes to area and volume to order the right quantity.'],'Wall 3.6 m by 2.7 m = 9.72 m2, minus a door 0.9 m by 2.1 m = 1.89 m2, gives 7.83 m2. Paint coverage 10 m2 per litre per coat, two coats: 15.7 m2 / 10 = 1.57 litres, plus 10% = 1.7 litres, so buy a 2-litre can.','Measure a wall and compute area, paint quantity and wastage.','Area and quantity are correct within 3% of the mentor check.','How much paint for 20 m2, two coats, 10 m2 per litre, plus 10%?','40 m2 divided by 10 is 4 litres, plus 10% is 4.4 litres.'),
 M('Diagnose a home problem','Analyse',5,['Describe the symptom, where and when it happens, and what changed recently.','List causes from most to least likely and test the simplest first.','Look for the source of dampness: leaking pipe, bad plaster, roof seepage or condensation.','Record findings with photos and measurements before fixing anything.'],'A wall patch of damp 60 cm wide at skirting height: closing the bathroom tap stops the growth; a moisture meter reads 25% near the pipe and 8% at 1 m away. Cause: leaking joint, not rising damp.','Diagnose one problem in a real or model room and write a findings sheet.','Sheet lists symptom, causes tested, evidence and the final cause.','Why test the simplest cause first?','It is quick, cheap and often the real cause.'),
 M('Do simple repairs','Apply',6,['Fix a dripping tap by closing the supply, replacing the washer, and testing for leaks.','Patch a small wall crack: clean, fill, let dry, sand and paint two coats.','Fix a door that sticks by tightening hinges, then planing only the rubbing edge.','Keep old parts, take photos of the steps and clean up the area afterwards.'],'Tap repair: valve closed, tap opened to drain, washer replaced for Rs 10, reassembled, tested for 10 minutes with no drips. Wall patch: filler, 24 hours drying, sand, 2 coats; total material Rs 180.','Complete two repairs with notes and before and after photos.','Repairs hold with no leak or crack after seven days.','Why shut the water supply before changing a washer?','To prevent flooding and to work on a dry fitting.'),
 M('Save energy and add smart devices','Evaluate',5,['Compare bulbs by watts and lumens; change old bulbs to LED to cut use by about 80%.','Add timers, motion sensors or smart plugs only after checking their load rating.','Use star ratings and the units used per day to compare fans, coolers and air conditioners.','Calculate payback as cost divided by yearly saving and choose items under 3 years.'],'Replace 10 bulbs of 60 W with 9 W LEDs: saving 51 W x 10 bulbs x 5 hours x 365 days = 931 kWh. At Rs 7 per unit that is Rs 6,517 a year. Cost Rs 1,000. Payback about 2 months.','Build an energy saving plan for one room with cost, saving and payback.','Plan shows load, units saved, rupees saved and payback for each change.','How do you calculate payback?','Divide the cost by the saving per year.'),
 M('Plan the job and write the quote','Create',6,['Write a scope: what is included, what is not, and the finish expected.','List materials with quantity, rate and total, adding 10% wastage; list labour by days.','Add a risk plan: isolation, PPE, dust and waste, protection of furniture and neighbours.','Itemise the quote with a payment schedule, start date and a warranty note.'],'Bathroom repaint and tap job: paint 3 litres Rs 1,350, filler Rs 150, washers and sealant Rs 220, labour 2 days x Rs 900 = Rs 1,800, contingency 10% Rs 352. Total Rs 3,872 with 30% advance.','Present a full job plan and quote for a real or model room.','Quote matches the materials list and schedule, with safety steps and exclusions stated.','Why itemise a quote?','So the customer sees what they are paying for and can check each line.')],
 extra=[('What is earthing for?','It carries fault current safely away so you do not get a shock.'),('Why add 10% wastage?','Cuts, breakage and mistakes use more material than the measured area.')],
 rubric=RUB('Planning','Correct measures, materials and schedule','Safety','Risks removed first and checked by a second person'),
 ladder=LAD('Know basic tools and home systems.','Explain how water, power and walls work.','Do simple repairs safely.','Run small jobs alone with quotes.','Lead renovations and manage trades.','Manage several projects and budgets.','Set standards for a contracting firm.'),
 jobs=['Handyman','Home service provider','Interior assistant','Small contractor','Facilities assistant']),
]
